However, if you want an iterative implementation that computes modular addition without using the built-in `%` operator, here's an alternative:

```dafny
function Modulus(a: nat, b: nat, n: nat): nat
  requires n > 0
  ensures Modulus(a, b, n) == (a + b) % n
{
  (a + b) % n
}

method ComputeModulus(a: nat, b: nat, n: nat) returns (result: nat)
  requires n > 0
  ensures result == (a + b) % n
{
  var sum := a + b;
  result := sum;

  while result >= n
    invariant result >= 0
    invariant (sum - result) % n == 0
    decreases result
  {
    result := result - n;
  }
}
```

