The main fixes I made:

1. Changed set comprehensions from `{x | x in primes}` to `set x | x in primes` - Dafny uses `set x | x in S` syntax for set comprehensions.

2. Fixed the type errors by properly creating sets from sequences using set comprehensions.

3. Removed the problematic `|` operator usage that was being interpreted as bitwise OR.

4. Changed postconditions that used set comprehensions to use universal quantifiers instead: `forall x :: x in primes ==> x != result` instead of `result !in {x | x in primes}`.

The code should now compile without the resolution/type errors.
