Looking at the previous Dafny code and the instructions, I notice the original code has a logical issue. The postcondition ensures `sorted <==> (forall i, j :: 0 <= i < j < arr.Length ==> arr[i] <= arr[j])`, which means the array is sorted in non-decreasing order. However, the implementation has a bug: it only checks consecutive elements but claims to verify the full sorted property.

Here's the corrected Dafny code with proper loop invariants:

```dafny
method isSorted(arr: array<int>) returns (sorted: bool)
  requires arr.Length > 0
  ensures sorted <==> (forall i, j :: 0 <= i < j < arr.Length ==> arr[i] <= arr[j])
{
  var i := 0;
  sorted := true;

  while i < arr.Length - 1
    invariant 0 <= i <= arr.Length - 1
    invariant sorted == (forall k, l :: 0 <= k < l <= i ==> arr[k] <= arr[l])
