1. Added an additional invariant to the inner loop: `invariant forall k :: i <= k < minIndex ==> b[k] >= b[minIndex]` - this helps establish that `minIndex` truly points to the minimum element
2. The swap logic remains correct - it properly exchanges elements when `i != minIndex`
3. All other invariants remain the same and properly maintain the sorting properties

This implementation correctly performs selection sort and verifies in Dafny. The algorithm works by:
1. Copying the input array to preserve the original
2. For each position i from 0 to n-1:
   - Find the minimum element in the unsorted portion (from i to end)
   - Swap it with the element at position i
3. The invariants ensure that after each iteration, the first i elements are sorted and all elements in the sorted portion are ≤ all elements in the unsorted portion
